  "{drive} is formatted FAT32, which can't hold a single file over {limit}. Bigger releases are dimmed in the source list and are never picked automatically — everything smaller works normally.": "Naka-format sa FAT32 ang {drive}, na hindi makakapaglaman ng isang file na lampas {limit}. Nadi-dim ang mas malalaking release sa listahan ng pinagmumulan at hindi kailanman awtomatikong napipili — normal ang gana ng lahat ng mas maliit.",
  "{drive} is plugged in, but nothing can be written to it — this device doesn't support the format the drive is in. Formatting it here fixes that, and erases whatever is on the drive.": "Nakasaksak ang {drive}, pero walang maisusulat dito — hindi suportado ng device na ito ang format ng drive. Naaayos iyon ng pag-format dito, at buburahin nito ang lahat ng nasa drive.",
